## 🇬🇧 **English description**

```markdown
# 🌌 3D N-Body Gravity Simulator

Interactive 3D simulation of gravitational interactions with eternal planetary trails.
The project demonstrates object motion in a solar system using 4th-order Runge-Kutta integration.

## 🌟 Features

- **N-body gravity** — all bodies interact with each other
- **Accurate integration** — Runge-Kutta 4th order (RK4)
- **Eternal trails** — unlimited length trails for planets
- **3D camera** — rotation, zoom, auto-rotation
- **Starry background** — 2000 twinkling stars with parallax
- **Asteroid belt** — 20 asteroids for visual enhancement
- **Time control** — speed up/slow down in real-time

## 🎮 Controls

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `← → ↑ ↓` | Rotate camera |
| `+ / -` | Zoom in/out |
| `R` | Toggle auto-rotation |
| `O` | Toggle trails |
| `C` | Clear all trails (start over) |
| `Space` | Pause/Resume |
| `[` | Slow down time |
| `]` | Speed up time |
| `ESC` | Exit |

## 🚀 Installation

```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/peacefullyyy/3d-Nbody-simulation.git
cd 3d-Nbody-simulation

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Run
python main.py
📦 Dependencies
Python 3.8+

Pygame 2.0+

NumPy 1.19+

🔧 Configuration
All simulation parameters in src/config.py:

python
G = 1.0              # Gravitational constant
SUN_MASS = 1000.0    # Sun mass
DT = 0.005           # Time step
🛠️ Technical Details
Integration: RK4 (Runge-Kutta 4th order)

Gravity: Newton's law of universal gravitation

Projection: Perspective 3D

Optimization: Trail projection caching

Trails: Unlimited length (eternal)

📁 Project Structure
text
3d-Nbody-simulation/
├── main.py              # Entry point
├── src/
│   ├── __init__.py      # Package init
│   ├── body.py          # Body class
│   ├── simulation.py    # Physics engine (RK4)
